  "findings": [
    "The first enabled original SVGOMG launch invoked no hint: all nine preparation checks reported ready. Mode selection alone does not establish invocation.",
    "The second enabled SVGOMG launch made five hints: all reported matched; four were followed by another error:unstable preparation retry and one by ready.",
    "The enabled controlled moving-target probe made 16 matched hints; 15 were followed by another error:unstable preparation retry. It made 18 preparation calls versus six in the separate ordinary probe. These counts expose repeated work; no elapsed or CPU saving is inferred.",
    "Both moving-target probes delivered exactly one trusted click after observed motion stopped, at the stopped target geometry. Fresh ordinary preparation still enforces input safety.",
    "Source inspection shows the hint compares geometry on successive condition checks, while the shared registry can run both mutation/event and frame checks. Those observations need not be distinct animation frames. This is a candidate explanation for early hints, not a captured proof of each wakeup source."
  ],
  "decision": "Keep hints opt-in. A frame-paced read-only hint is a possible follow-up, subject to cancellation/fairness/fresh input checks and a new complete-work screen. Do not attribute earlier uninstrumented screen regressions to hint overhead without invocation evidence.",
